{
  "slug": "mediacontrol",
  "name": "MediaControl",
  "tagline": "A now-playing panel for Minecraft: album cover, title, progress bar and play/pause/skip for whatever you are listening to.",
  "icon": "/assets/mediacontrol.png",
  "side": "Client",
  "categories": [
    "Utility",
    "Client"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "links": {},
  "description": [
    "MediaControl adds a **now-playing panel** to the Minecraft pause menu and main menu. It shows the album cover, title and artist, elapsed and total time, a scrubbable progress bar, and play/pause, previous and next buttons for whatever you are listening to on your computer. Spotify, browsers, VLC and most other players work.",
    {
      "heading": "Features"
    },
    {
      "list": [
        "Works with your system-wide media: Windows media controls (SMTC) or Linux MPRIS",
        "Panel on the pause menu and in the bottom-left of the main menu",
        "A toast slides up when the track changes, then shows \"Press [Esc] to control\"",
        "Scrub the progress bar to seek, plus play/pause and skip buttons",
        "Accent color changeable by hex code in Mod Menu (default #0080FF)",
        "Client-side only: nothing is needed on servers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Linux"
    },
    "Windows needs nothing extra. On Linux you need **`playerctl`** and a media player that supports MPRIS (Spotify, VLC, Firefox, Chrome and most others do).",
    {
      "list": [
        "Ubuntu / Debian / Mint: `sudo apt install playerctl`",
        "Fedora: `sudo dnf install playerctl`",
        "Arch / Manjaro: `sudo pacman -S playerctl`",
        "openSUSE: `sudo zypper install playerctl`",
        "Check it works while music plays: `playerctl --list-all` should list your player",
        "Flatpak launchers (Prism, Modrinth App): also run `flatpak override --user --talk-name=org.freedesktop.Flatpak <launcher app id>`, for example `org.prismlauncher.PrismLauncher` or `com.modrinth.ModrinthApp`, then restart the launcher"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Good to know"
    },
    {
      "list": [
        "The mod starts one small helper process to read and control your media player. It only reads what is playing and sends playback commands; the only network request is downloading the current album cover from the address your player provides.",
        "Supported systems are Windows and Linux. On other systems the panel shows \"Incompatible Operating System\".",
        "Each download covers a range of Minecraft versions; pick your loader and version and the site gives you the right file."
      ]
    }
  ],
